# What never leaves this machine.
#
# This is the control that actually works: `excludeFiles` in vercel.json is not honored
# by the zero-config Flask preset (verified with `vercel build` — the bundle was
# byte-identical with and without it), so anything that must stay out has to be listed
# here, where it is dropped from the upload itself.
#
# A Git-connected deploy only ever uploads tracked files, so the secrets below are
# already safe there. This covers `vercel deploy` run from a working directory.

# Secrets and real data. `.env` holds live credentials and instance/ holds the local
# database and uploaded media.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
instance/

# Never needed at runtime.
tests/
plans/
docs/
scripts/tn_oauth.py
scripts/tn_spike.py
scripts/local-docker-debug.sh

# Local clutter.
ig-gluck_bags/
relevamiento-seo-*/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.vercel/
_uv/
Jenkinsfile
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile

# NOT ignored on purpose: app/static/** (the build copies it into public/ for the CDN)
# and requirements.txt (the build installs from it).
